Yes, that's the clean route. Have your lawyer send the preservation letter today, and make sure it:

- names the camera (parking lot / pickup loop) and the specific dates and pickup times from your log within the last 30 days, plus all pickups from now until the case is resolved;
- mentions the custody proceedings, since that's what triggers their policy;
- asks the school to confirm in writing that the footage has been preserved.

Then let discovery or a subpoena get the copies; once the footage is preserved, the 4-6 weeks no longer matters. A quick call to the office manager to check the letter arrived is fine, but don't ask her for the clips. And keep logging, so each date lines up with what the footage shows.
